<div id="applications" style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:28px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:90px;"><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 8px;">Applications</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:660px;margin:0 0 16px;">The same packages and modules are built for different end uses. These pages cover each application.</p><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;"><a href="/markets/automotive/power-modules" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="text-decoration:none;">Automotive power modules <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a><a href="/markets/industrial-iot/power-modules" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="text-decoration:none;">Industrial power modules <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a><a href="/markets/power-management" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="text-decoration:none;">Power management market <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a></div></div>
</div></div>
<div style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Where we run it</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Power package assembly is available across our OSAT network; production mix varies by site.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-4"><a href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">Thailand</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Ayutthaya</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Ayutthaya <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">China</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Jiaxing</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Jiaxing <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;"><details class="sc-faq" open><summary>Which module formats do you assemble?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">34 mm, 62 mm, EconoDual 3, Econo, PIM, Easy 1B, 2B and 3B, and HP1 and HPD for traction inverters, plus SiC on DBC built into a custom SiP where a standard format does not fit.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Which power discretes are AEC-Q101 qualified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">The TO-247 family (2L, 3L, 4L and 4L notched), D2PAK-7L and TSPAK are AEC-Q101 qualified. TOLL and PQFN 8×8 are qualified to industrial requirements. Maximum die size for each package is listed in the power package reference above and can be adjusted after design and process evaluation.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>How do you manage thermal performance in a wide-bandgap package?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Copper clip interconnect instead of wire bonds, dual-cooled pads exposed top and bottom, and ceramic DBC substrates. Voids in the thermal path are held under 5% by vacuum reflow.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What voltage and isolation class can you assemble to?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Devices to the 1200 V class, with built-in isolation above 2500 V on the TO-247TE outline.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Do you package GaN devices?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. GaN devices can be packaged in power QFN 5×6 and in custom IPMs for battery chargers, SiP power converters and EV chargers, including GaN and SiC on DBC. Laser grooving and dicing are qualified for SiC and GaN wafers.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What reliability testing can you run on a power module?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Power cycling, thermal cycling and reliability sequences are available to the programme qualification plan. The test set is agreed per programme and confirmed per site.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What is this used for?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">EV and hybrid drivetrains, rail traction, solar and wind inverters, industrial drives, and data center power.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Can you build a module footprint that isn't one of the standards?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. SiC on DBC assembled into a custom SiP. If the outline itself has to be drawn, that runs through package design and simulation before any tooling is cut.</div></details></div></div></div></div>
